<section class="panel cp-span-full">
    <h2>Classic+ FAQ</h2>
    <ul class="plain-list">
        <li><strong>What is WoW Classic Plus?</strong> The community name for a potential Classic WoW that keeps the original foundation while adding new content, progression or systems. No official product named "Classic Plus" exists.</li>
        <li><strong>What is Project Camelot?</strong> An unannounced WoW project name tied through datamining to an encrypted 1.60 development branch. Its public name, features and purpose are unconfirmed.</li>
        <li><strong>Is Camelot confirmed as Classic+?</strong> No — it is the leading community theory, but Blizzard has not confirmed the connection.</li>
        <li><strong>What is the mysterious Patch 1.60 build?</strong> An encrypted WoW development branch on Blizzard infrastructure. The version number does not reveal its content or release model.</li>
        <li><strong>Does Patch 1.60.1 prove a beta or release date?</strong> No. It confirms continued development on a point-one branch beyond 1.60.0 — nothing more.</li>
        <li><strong>Is Camelot still being developed?</strong> Yes — build updates on both 1.60.0 and 1.60.1 branches as of August 15, 2026, though the builds remain encrypted.</li>
        <li><strong>Will Classic+ stay at level 60?</strong> Unconfirmed. Many players favor a permanent level-60 endgame, but Patch 1.60 does not prove that design.</li>
        <li><strong>Permanent or seasonal?</strong> Unannounced. It could be a long-term branch, another experimental season, or a different kind of WoW product.</li>
        <li><strong>How would Classic+ differ from Season of Discovery?</strong> SoD is a seasonal Classic with altered progression and new abilities; Classic+ is imagined as a broader, possibly permanent expansion of the original game.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="meta-info">FAQ compiled from community discussion and available reporting.</p>
</section>

